  "method_step": 5,
  "operation": "single-vector-chance-loop",
  "status": "declared_pending_independent_whole_build_review",
  "declared_at": "2026-11-15T22:18:45.829564-06:00",
  "why_this_direction": "The one-reference computational observable, predictive vector chance and joint inverse are implemented. The missing native connection is now built: use the same one originally wrong prompt, update all editable matrices jointly, acquire its complete native trace again and repeat until the identical original boundary closes. This executes the established method rather than selecting another calibration form.",
  "repeating_pattern_check": "Earlier runs followed text, state targets or partial surrogates; recent discussion also inferred an obstruction from shared prompt positions. This run compares only the full input-output computational relation. No position, shared wording, favorable generated output or old scalar trend selects support, changes chance or establishes closure. Held-history Torch values select only proposals; fresh native regeneration judges the reached state.",
  "hypothesis": "Repeated joint inverse corrections from complete fresh native computational traces can bring the selected failing prompt inside the unchanged original predictive vector boundary at every compared merge.",
  "what_went_wrong_before": "Component-box diagnostics and earlier state/Taylor objectives are not reused. The fixed original observed trace and original-only computational correspondence remain; no token comparison supplies the loss, correspondence cost, scope or stopping.",
  "rule": "Observe one full native trace from the current BF16 model. Pair complete full-turn fields chronologically with the fixed original reference. Compute the radial residual beyond sqrt(2C), with original-event mass. Hold these pairs for joint CGLS over all model attention-output and feed-forward-down matrices. Derive trial length from the whole response and search distinct native BF16 proposals on the anchored held-history graph. Publish a complete accepted joint state, regenerate the same prompt on that file and refresh pairing/measurement. Continue without an iteration cap; initial agreement, incomplete acquisition or numerical stagnation is not closure. After at least one update and fresh complete zero-excess trace, publish closure and separately declare the preselected other fitting-prompt evaluation.",
  "prediction": "Each accepted inverse proposal produces a completely installed BF16 state followed by a newly acquired native trace. Repeated native remeasurement reaches zero outside cells against exactly the original vector chance, without output grading.",
  "would_weaken_it": "Initial native zero excess supplies no repair request. A nonzero residual with numerical stationarity, no improving distinct BF16 proposal, incomplete generation, or failure of continued native excess to close weakens this construction; none is relabeled closure or repaired by a new floor/reference/support. Post-closure fitting transfer may fail even when the one trace closes.",
